Subject: [PATCH 11027/11171] Refresh the handoff: the induce run finished, and
 five decisions are waiting

ops/status.md's newest block described the r11l run as in progress with one
engine. It finished at 07:49Z with four, so a successor reading the handoff
document got a stale picture of the one thing that mattered most. Appended
rather than edited, per never-prune, with a pointer saying which block to read.

Also captures a decision that existed only in conversation and would have been
lost: the r11l tools A/B is measured and the flag ledger still cannot see it,
even though the ledger gained a --record-null path the same day. The exact
commands are in the entry, because "there is a way to record this" is not the
same as "here is how", and the difference is whether it happens.

Lists the other four operator decisions in one place -- ledger migration, the
stamp-order choice, whether to harden the ARC floor lint, and the seven
SILENT_NON_FIRING findings against adversarial_verify -- plus the four things
filed and deliberately not built, so the open set is readable without
reconstructing it from a day of commits.

Written on the hourly what-is-not-written pass, which is what surfaced that the
handoff document was describing yesterday.

